[2026-03-14T19:33:11.406Z] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Gie44JwuzNh6QcYW69jjpg","type":"tool_result","content":"   100→- **Expected:** The property grid updates to show only properties where the city matches \"Paris\". Properties in other cities are not displayed.\n   101→\n   102→#### Test: Search by check-in and check-out dates filters results\n   103→- **Initial state:** User is on the home page. Some properties have bookings that overlap with the selected dates.\n   104→- **Action:** User selects a check-in date of \"2026-04-01\" and a check-out date of \"2026-04-05\" using the date pickers, then clicks the search button.\n   105→- **Expected:** The property grid updates to show only properties that are available (not fully booked) for the selected date range. The date pickers display the selected dates in a readable format.\n   106→\n   107→#### Test: Search by guest count filters results\n   108→- **Initial state:** User is on the home page. Properties exist with max_guests values of 2, 4, and 8.\n   109→- **Action:** User sets the guest count to 5 and clicks the search button.\n   110→- **Expected:** The property grid updates to show only properties where max_guests >= 5. Properties with fewer guest capacity are hidden.\n   111→\n   112→#### Test: Combined search with all fields filters results\n   113→- **Initial state:** User is on the home page. Multiple properties exist with varying locations, availability, and guest capacities.\n   114→- **Action:** User types \"New York\" in the location field, selects check-in \"2026-05-10\" and check-out \"2026-05-15\", sets guests to 3, and clicks the search button.\n   115→- **Expected:** The property grid shows only properties in New York that are available for those dates and accommodate at least 3 guests.\n   116→\n   117→#### Test: Clearing search fields and re-searching shows all results\n   118→- **Initial state:** User has performed a search for \"Paris\" and the grid shows filtered results.\n   119→- **Action:** User clears the location field (making it empty) and clicks the search button.\n   120→- **Expected:** The property grid resets to show all properties (unfiltered by location).\n   121→\n   122→#### Test: Search bar is functional on repeated use\n   123→- **Initial state:** User is on the home page.\n   124→- **Action:** User searches for \"Paris\", views results, then clears the location field, types \"Tokyo\", and searches again.\n   125→- **Expected:** The first search shows only Paris properties. After the second search, the grid updates to show only Tokyo properties. The location input correctly reflects \"Tokyo\".\n   126→\n   127→#### Test: Check-in date picker prevents selecting past dates\n   128→- **Initial state:** User is on the home page.\n   129→- **Action:** User opens the check-in date picker.\n   130→- **Expected:** Dates before today are disabled/grayed out and cannot be selected.\n   131→\n   132→#### Test: Check-out date must be after check-in date\n   133→- **Initial state:** User is on the home page and has selected a check-in date of \"2026-04-10\".\n   134→- **Action:** User opens the check-out date picker.\n   135→- **Expected:** Dates on or before \"2026-04-10\" are disabled/grayed out and cannot be selected. Only dates after the check-in date are selectable.\n   136→\n   137→#### Test: Guest count selector enforces minimum of 1\n   138→- **Initial state:** User is on the home page.\n   139→- **Action:** User interacts with the guest count selector.\n   140→- **Expected:** The minimum selectable value is 1. The user cannot set the guest count to 0 or a negative number.\n   141→\n   142→### Component: CategoryFilter\n   143→\n   144→#### Test: Category filter bar displays all property type chips\n   145→- **Initial state:** User navigates to the home page (`/`).\n   146→- **Expected:** A horizontal scrollable bar of category chips is displayed below the search bar. Chips are shown for each property type: \"Apartment\", \"House\", \"Cabin\", \"Villa\", \"Condo\", \"Loft\", \"Cottage\", \"Townhouse\". No chip is selected by default (all properties are shown).\n   147→\n   148→#### Test: Clicking a category chip filters properties by that type\n   149→- **Initial state:** User is on the home page. Properties of various types exist (apartments, houses, cabins, etc.).\n   150→- **Action:** User clicks the \"Cabin\" chip.\n   151→- **Expected:** The \"Cabin\" chip becomes visually selected/highlighted (e.g., bold outline or filled background). The property grid updates to show only properties with property_type \"Cabin\".\n   152→\n   153→#### Test: Clicking the selected category chip deselects it and shows all properties\n   154→- **Initial state:** User is on the home page with the \"Cabin\" chip currently selected.\n   155→- **Action:** User clicks the \"Cabin\" chip again.\n   156→- **Expected:** The \"Cabin\" chip returns to its unselected appearance. The property grid shows all properties again (no category filter applied).\n   157→\n   158→#### Test: Switching between category chips updates the filter\n   159→- **Initial state:** User is on the home page with the \"Cabin\" chip selected, showing only cabin properties.\n   160→- **Action:** User clicks the \"Villa\" chip.\n   161→- **Expected:** The \"Cabin\" chip becomes unselected and the \"Villa\" chip becomes selected/highlighted. The property grid updates to show only properties with property_type \"Villa\".\n   162→\n   163→#### Test: Category filter works in combination with search bar\n   164→- **Initial state:** User is on the home page. Properties exist: a cabin in Paris, an apartment in Paris, and a cabin in Tokyo.\n   165→- **Action:** User types \"Paris\" in the search bar location field and clicks search, then clicks the \"Cabin\" chip.\n   166→- **Expected:** The property grid shows only cabin properties in Paris. Both the search and category filters are applied simultaneously.\n   167→\n   168→#### Test: Category filter bar is horizontally scrollable when chips overflow\n   169→- **Initial state:** User is on the home page on a narrow viewport where all chips don't fit in one row.\n   170→- **Expected:** The category filter bar is horizontally scrollable. The user can scroll left/right to see all property type chips.\n   171→\n   172→#### Test: Category chip is functional on repeated use\n   173→- **Initial state:** User is on the home page.\n   174→- **Action:** User clicks \"Apartment\" (filtered), then clicks \"House\" (switches filter), then clicks \"House\" again (deselects), then clicks \"Cabin\" (filtered again).\n   175→- **Expected:** Each click correctly updates the selected chip and the property grid filters. The final state shows only cabin properties with the \"Cabin\" chip highlighted.\n   176→\n   177→### Component: PropertyGrid\n   178→\n   179→#### Test: Property grid displays properties in a responsive grid layout\n   180→- **Initial state:** User navigates to the home page. Multiple properties exist in the database.\n   181→- **Expected:** Properties are displayed in a responsive grid: 1 column on mobile, 2 columns on tablet, 3-4 columns on desktop. Each property is rendered as a PropertyCard.\n   182→\n   183→#### Test: Property grid shows message when no properties match filters\n   184→- **Initial state:** User is on the home page.\n   185→- **Action:** User searches for a location with no matching properties (e.g., \"Atlantis\").\n   186→- **Expected:** The property grid area displays a \"No properties found\" message instead of an empty grid. The message suggests adjusting filters or search criteria.\n   187→\n   188→#### Test: Property grid loads and displays properties from API on initial page load\n   189→- **Initial state:** User navigates to the home page. Properties exist in the database.\n   190→- **Expected:** The grid fetches properties via `GET /api/properties` and displays property cards. While loading, a loading indicator is shown. Once loaded, the property cards appear with correct data.\n   191→\n   192→### Component: PropertyCard\n   193→\n   194→#### Test: Property card displays all required information\n   195→- **Initial state:** User is on the home page. A property exists with title \"Cozy Cabin\", city \"Aspen\", country \"US\", property_type \"Cabin\", price_per_night 150, an average rating of 4.5, and 12 reviews.\n   196→- **Expected:** The property card shows: the main property image at the top, a \"Cabin\" property type badge, the title \"Cozy Cabin\", location \"Aspen, US\", \"$150 / night\" price, and a star icon with \"4.5 (12 reviews)\" rating display.\n   197→\n   198→#### Test: Property card shows property image\n   199→- **Initial state:** User is on the home page. A property exists with at least one image (the first image by display_order).\n   200→- **Expected:** The property card displays the main image (lowest display_order) at the top of the card with rounded top corners. If no image exists, a placeholder image is shown.\n   201→\n   202→#### Test: Clicking a property card navigates to property detail page\n   203→- **Initial state:** User is on the home page. A property with id \"abc-123\" is displayed.\n   204→- **Action:** User clicks on the property card (not the favorite button).\n   205→- **Expected:** The app navigates to `/properties/abc-123` (the property detail page).\n   206→\n   207→#### Test: Property card displays property type badge\n   208→- **Initial state:** User is on the home page. Properties of different types exist.\n   209→- **Expected:** Each property card shows a badge/label indicating the property type (e.g., \"Apartment\", \"House\", \"Cabin\"). The badge is visually distinct (e.g., small colored label overlaying or near the image).\n   210→\n   211→#### Test: Property card displays average rating with review count\n   212→- **Initial state:** User is on the home page. A property has an average rating of 4.2 from 8 reviews.\n   213→- **Expected:** The card shows a star icon with \"4.2\" and \"(8 reviews)\" or \"(8)\" next to it. If the property has no reviews, the rating section shows \"New\" or is not displayed.\n   214→\n   215→### Component: FavoriteButton\n   216→\n   217→#### Test: Favorite button shows outline heart when property is not favorited\n   218→- **Initial state:** User is logged in and on the home page. The property is not in the user's favorites.\n   219→- **Expected:** The property card displays a heart icon with an outline (unfilled) style in the top-right corner of the card image.\n   220→\n   221→#### Test: Clicking favorite button on unfavorited property adds it to favorites\n   222→- **Initial state:** User is logged in and on the home page. A property is not in their favorites.\n   223→- **Action:** User clicks the heart icon on the property card.\n   224→- **Expected:** The app calls `POST /api/favorites` with the property ID. The heart icon changes to a filled/solid red heart. The property is now in the user's favorites list.\n   225→\n   226→#### Test: Clicking favorite button on favorited property removes it from favorites\n   227→- **Initial state:** User is logged in and on the home page. A property is already in their favorites (heart is filled/red).\n   228→- **Action:** User clicks the filled heart icon on the property card.\n   229→- **Expected:** The app calls `DELETE /api/favorites/:propertyId`. The heart icon changes back to an outline (unfilled) style. The property is removed from the user's favorites.\n   230→\n   231→#### Test: Favorite button does not navigate to property detail page\n   232→- **Initial state:** User is logged in and on the home page.\n   233→- **Action:** User clicks the heart icon on a property card.\n   234→- **Expected:** The favorite is toggled but the user remains on the home page. The click does not propagate to the card's navigation handler.\n   235→\n   236→#### Test: Favorite button is not shown when user is not logged in\n   237→- **Initial state:** User is not logged in and is on the home page.\n   238→- **Expected:** Property cards do not display the heart/favorite icon. Alternatively, clicking the heart redirects the user to the login page.\n   239→\n   240→#### Test: Favorite button reflects correct state on page load\n   241→- **Initial state:** User is logged in and has previously favorited two properties. User navigates to the home page.\n   242→- **Expected:** The app calls `GET /api/favorites` to fetch the user's favorites. The two favorited properties show filled/red hearts. All other properties show outline hearts.\n   243→\n   244→#### Test: Favorite button is functional on repeated use\n   245→- **Initial state:** User is logged in and on the home page with a property that is not favorited.\n   246→- **Action:** User clicks the heart icon (favorites it), then clicks it again (unfavorites it), then clicks it a third time (favorites it again).\n   247→- **Expected:** Each click correctly toggles the heart appearance and makes the appropriate API call. The final state is favorited (filled heart).\n   248→\n   249→### Component: FiltersPanel\n   250→\n   251→#### Test: Filters panel is hidden by default with a visible toggle button\n   252→- **Initial state:** User navigates to the home page (`/`).\n   253→- **Expected:** The filters panel is collapsed/hidden. A \"Filters\" button (with a filter icon) is visible that the user can click to open the panel.\n   254→\n   255→#### Test: Clicking the Filters button opens the filters panel\n   256→- **Initial state:** User is on the home page with the filters panel hidden.\n   257→- **Action:** User clicks the \"Filters\" button.\n   258→- **Expected:** The filters panel opens/expands, revealing all filter controls: a price range slider, bedrooms minimum selector, beds minimum selector, bathrooms minimum selector, and amenity checkboxes grouped by category.\n   259→\n   260→#### Test: Clicking the Filters button again closes the filters panel\n   261→- **Initial state:** User is on the home page with the filters panel open.\n   262→- **Action:** User clicks the \"Filters\" button again.\n   263→- **Expected:** The filters panel collapses/hides. The property grid remains showing the previously applied filters.\n   264→\n   265→#### Test: Price range slider filters properties by price per night\n   266→- **Initial state:** User is on the home page with the filters panel open. Properties exist with prices $50, $100, $200, and $500 per night.\n   267→- **Action:** User adjusts the price range slider to a minimum of $75 and a maximum of $250.\n   268→- **Expected:** The property grid updates to show only properties with price_per_night between $75 and $250 (i.e., $100 and $200 properties). The slider visually reflects the selected range with labels showing the min and max values.\n   269→\n   270→#### Test: Bedrooms minimum filter works correctly\n   271→- **Initial state:** User is on the home page with the filters panel open. Properties exist with 1, 2, 3, and 5 bedrooms.\n   272→- **Action:** User sets the bedrooms minimum selector to 3.\n   273→- **Expected:** The property grid updates to show only properties with 3 or more bedrooms.\n   274→\n   275→#### Test: Beds minimum filter works correctly\n   276→- **Initial state:** User is on the home page with the filters panel open. Properties exist with varying bed counts.\n   277→- **Action:** User sets the beds minimum selector to 2.\n   278→- **Expected:** The property grid updates to show only properties with 2 or more beds.\n   279→\n   280→#### Test: Bathrooms minimum filter works correctly\n   281→- **Initial state:** User is on the home page with the filters panel open. Properties exist with 1, 2, and 3 bathrooms.\n   282→- **Action:** User sets the bathrooms minimum selector to 2.\n   283→- **Expected:** The property grid updates to show only properties with 2 or more bathrooms.\n   284→\n   285→#### Test: Amenity checkboxes filter properties by selected amenities\n   286→- **Initial state:** User is on the home page with the filters panel open. Amenities include \"WiFi\", \"Pool\", \"Kitchen\", \"Parking\". Properties have varying amenities.\n   287→- **Action:** User checks the \"WiFi\" and \"Pool\" amenity checkboxes.\n   288→- **Expected:** The property grid updates to show only properties that have both WiFi AND Pool amenities. The checked amenities remain visually checked.\n   289→\n   290→#### Test: Amenity checkboxes are grouped by category\n   291→- **Initial state:** User is on the home page with the filters panel open.\n   292→- **Expected:** Amenity checkboxes are organized into groups labeled by category: \"Essentials\", \"Features\", \"Safety\", \"Location\". Each group contains the relevant amenities.\n   293→\n   294→#### Test: Multiple filters combine with AND logic\n   295→- **Initial state:** User is on the home page with the filters panel open.\n   296→- **Action:** User sets price range to $100–$300, bedrooms minimum to 2, and checks the \"WiFi\" amenity.\n   297→- **Expected:** The property grid shows only properties that satisfy ALL three conditions: price between $100–$300, at least 2 bedrooms, and has WiFi amenity.\n   298→\n   299→#### Test: Filters combine with search bar and category filter"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01XeEJo91zX1zVTTDE8kgZQi","session_id":"428f3191-9775-460c-8316-8366502bc989","uuid":"6665f881-c3a6-4394-90bd-b9865c6244cd"}
