[2026-03-14T19:33:20.410Z] {"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01DF8S99DFb1LbSPDKVok2T3","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01YWnydAPU2RZGzfccCrXwKV","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/repo/apps/AirbnbClone/docs/tests.md","offset":300,"limit":200},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2378,"cache_read_input_tokens":33366,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2378,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01XeEJo91zX1zVTTDE8kgZQi","session_id":"428f3191-9775-460c-8316-8366502bc989","uuid":"1cc1a7a5-11d2-411e-9506-3a552ae9f353"}
[2026-03-14T19:33:20.620Z] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01YWnydAPU2RZGzfccCrXwKV","type":"tool_result","content":"   300→- **Initial state:** User is on the home page. User has typed \"Paris\" in the search bar, selected \"Apartment\" category chip, and the filters panel is open.\n   301→- **Action:** User sets bedrooms minimum to 2 in the filters panel.\n   302→- **Expected:** The property grid shows only apartments in Paris with at least 2 bedrooms. All three filter mechanisms (search, category, filters panel) work together.\n   303→\n   304→#### Test: Resetting filters shows all properties\n   305→- **Initial state:** User is on the home page with multiple filters applied (price range, bedrooms, amenities).\n   306→- **Action:** User resets or clears all filter values back to their defaults (e.g., via a \"Clear Filters\" or \"Reset\" button, or manually resetting each).\n   307→- **Expected:** The property grid returns to showing all properties (unfiltered). All filter controls return to their default states.\n   308→\n   309→#### Test: Filters panel controls are functional on repeated use\n   310→- **Initial state:** User is on the home page with the filters panel open.\n   311→- **Action:** User sets bedrooms to 3 (filtered), then changes bedrooms back to 1, then sets bathrooms to 2, then unchecks and re-checks a \"WiFi\" amenity.\n   312→- **Expected:** Each change updates the property grid correctly. The final state reflects the last set of filter values (bedrooms >= 1, bathrooms >= 2, WiFi checked).\n   313→\n   314→### Component: Pagination\n   315→\n   316→#### Test: Pagination controls are displayed when results exceed one page\n   317→- **Initial state:** User is on the home page. More properties exist than can fit on one page (e.g., more than the page limit of 12 or 20 properties).\n   318→- **Expected:** Pagination controls are displayed below the property grid showing page numbers (e.g., \"1 2 3 ... 5\"), a \"Previous\" button (disabled on first page), and a \"Next\" button.\n   319→\n   320→#### Test: Pagination controls are hidden when all results fit on one page\n   321→- **Initial state:** User is on the home page. Fewer properties exist than the page limit.\n   322→- **Expected:** No pagination controls are displayed below the property grid.\n   323→\n   324→#### Test: Clicking Next page loads the next set of properties\n   325→- **Initial state:** User is on the home page viewing page 1 of results. Multiple pages of properties exist.\n   326→- **Action:** User clicks the \"Next\" button.\n   327→- **Expected:** The property grid updates to show the second page of properties. The URL or API call includes `page=2`. The current page indicator highlights \"2\". The \"Previous\" button becomes enabled.\n   328→\n   329→#### Test: Clicking Previous page loads the previous set of properties\n   330→- **Initial state:** User is on page 2 of property results.\n   331→- **Action:** User clicks the \"Previous\" button.\n   332→- **Expected:** The property grid updates to show the first page of properties. The current page indicator highlights \"1\". The \"Previous\" button becomes disabled again.\n   333→\n   334→#### Test: Clicking a specific page number navigates to that page\n   335→- **Initial state:** User is on page 1 of results. At least 3 pages of properties exist.\n   336→- **Action:** User clicks page number \"3\".\n   337→- **Expected:** The property grid updates to show the third page of properties. The current page indicator highlights \"3\".\n   338→\n   339→#### Test: Next button is disabled on the last page\n   340→- **Initial state:** User is on the last page of property results.\n   341→- **Expected:** The \"Next\" button is disabled/grayed out and not clickable. The \"Previous\" button is enabled.\n   342→\n   343→#### Test: Previous button is disabled on the first page\n   344→- **Initial state:** User is on page 1 of property results.\n   345→- **Expected:** The \"Previous\" button is disabled/grayed out and not clickable. The \"Next\" button is enabled (if more than one page exists).\n   346→\n   347→#### Test: Applying filters resets pagination to page 1\n   348→- **Initial state:** User is on page 3 of property results.\n   349→- **Action:** User applies a category filter by clicking the \"Cabin\" chip.\n   350→- **Expected:** The pagination resets to page 1. The property grid shows the first page of filtered results. The page indicator highlights \"1\".\n   351→\n   352→#### Test: Pagination is functional on repeated use\n   353→- **Initial state:** User is on page 1 of results with multiple pages available.\n   354→- **Action:** User clicks \"Next\" (goes to page 2), then clicks \"Next\" again (page 3), then clicks \"Previous\" (back to page 2), then clicks page \"1\" (back to page 1).\n   355→- **Expected:** Each navigation correctly updates the property grid and page indicator. The final state shows page 1 results.\n   356→\n   357→## Page: Property Detail (`/properties/:id`)\n   358→\n   359→<!-- Components: ImageGallery, PropertyHeader, PropertyInfo, PropertyDescription, AmenitiesList, BookingCard, ReviewsSection, HostInfoCard -->\n   360→\n   361→### Component: ImageGallery\n   362→\n   363→#### Test: Image gallery displays main large image and smaller thumbnails\n   364→- **Initial state:** User navigates to `/properties/:id` for a property with 5 images.\n   365→- **Expected:** The image gallery shows a grid layout with the first image (lowest display_order) displayed as a large main image, and the remaining images displayed as smaller thumbnails alongside or below it. All images have rounded corners.\n   366→\n   367→#### Test: Image gallery displays single image when property has only one image\n   368→- **Initial state:** User navigates to a property detail page for a property with exactly 1 image.\n   369→- **Expected:** The single image is displayed as the main large image. No thumbnail grid is shown.\n   370→\n   371→#### Test: Image gallery displays placeholder when property has no images\n   372→- **Initial state:** User navigates to a property detail page for a property with no images.\n   373→- **Expected:** A placeholder image or \"No images available\" message is displayed in the gallery area.\n   374→\n   375→#### Test: Clicking a thumbnail image makes it the main displayed image\n   376→- **Initial state:** User is on a property detail page with 5 images. The first image is displayed as the main image.\n   377→- **Action:** User clicks on the third thumbnail image.\n   378→- **Expected:** The third image becomes the main large image. The previously main image moves to the thumbnail grid.\n   379→\n   380→#### Test: Clicking thumbnails is functional on repeated use\n   381→- **Initial state:** User is on a property detail page with multiple images.\n   382→- **Action:** User clicks the second thumbnail, then the fourth thumbnail, then the first thumbnail.\n   383→- **Expected:** Each click updates the main image to the clicked thumbnail. The final state shows the first thumbnail as the main image.\n   384→\n   385→#### Test: Image gallery shows image captions when available\n   386→- **Initial state:** User navigates to a property detail page. The property has images with caption text set.\n   387→- **Expected:** Captions are displayed below or overlaying their respective images.\n   388→\n   389→### Component: PropertyHeader\n   390→\n   391→#### Test: Property header displays title, location, rating summary, and host info\n   392→- **Initial state:** User navigates to `/properties/:id` for a property with title \"Luxury Villa in Bali\", city \"Ubud\", country \"Indonesia\", an average rating of 4.7 from 23 reviews, hosted by \"Jane Host\" with an avatar.\n   393→- **Expected:** The property header shows the title \"Luxury Villa in Bali\", location \"Ubud, Indonesia\", a star icon with \"4.7\" and \"(23 reviews)\", and the host name \"Jane Host\" with their avatar image.\n   394→\n   395→#### Test: Property header shows \"New\" when property has no reviews\n   396→- **Initial state:** User navigates to a property detail page for a property with no reviews.\n   397→- **Expected:** The rating summary area shows \"New\" or no rating display instead of a numeric rating and review count.\n   398→\n   399→#### Test: Clicking review count scrolls to or navigates to reviews section\n   400→- **Initial state:** User is on a property detail page with reviews.\n   401→- **Action:** User clicks the \"(23 reviews)\" link in the property header.\n   402→- **Expected:** The page scrolls down to the ReviewsSection on the same page.\n   403→\n   404→#### Test: Property header displays host avatar as clickable element\n   405→- **Initial state:** User is on a property detail page. The host has an avatar_url set.\n   406→- **Expected:** The host's avatar image is displayed as a small circular image next to the host name. The host name is displayed next to the avatar.\n   407→\n   408→### Component: PropertyInfo\n   409→\n   410→#### Test: Property info section displays all property details\n   411→- **Initial state:** User navigates to `/properties/:id` for a property with property_type \"Villa\", max_guests 6, bedrooms 3, beds 4, bathrooms 2.\n   412→- **Expected:** The property info section displays: \"Villa\" as the property type, \"6 guests\", \"3 bedrooms\", \"4 beds\", and \"2 bathrooms\". Each detail has an appropriate icon.\n   413→\n   414→#### Test: Property info section displays check-in and check-out times\n   415→- **Initial state:** User navigates to a property detail page for a property with check_in_time \"15:00\" and check_out_time \"11:00\".\n   416→- **Expected:** The property info section shows check-in time as \"3:00 PM\" (or \"15:00\") and check-out time as \"11:00 AM\" (or \"11:00\").\n   417→\n   418→#### Test: Property info section handles singular and plural labels correctly\n   419→- **Initial state:** User navigates to a property detail page for a property with max_guests 1, bedrooms 1, beds 1, bathrooms 1.\n   420→- **Expected:** Labels display in singular form: \"1 guest\", \"1 bedroom\", \"1 bed\", \"1 bathroom\" (not \"1 guests\", etc.).\n   421→\n   422→### Component: PropertyDescription\n   423→\n   424→#### Test: Property description displays full description text\n   425→- **Initial state:** User navigates to `/properties/:id` for a property with a multi-paragraph description.\n   426→- **Expected:** The full property description text is displayed in a readable format with proper paragraph breaks.\n   427→\n   428→#### Test: Long description shows a \"Show more\" toggle\n   429→- **Initial state:** User navigates to a property detail page for a property with a very long description (multiple paragraphs).\n   430→- **Expected:** The description is initially truncated after a reasonable length with a \"Show more\" link/button visible at the bottom.\n   431→\n   432→#### Test: Clicking \"Show more\" expands the full description\n   433→- **Initial state:** User is on a property detail page with a truncated description and a visible \"Show more\" link.\n   434→- **Action:** User clicks the \"Show more\" link.\n   435→- **Expected:** The full description expands to show all text. The link changes to \"Show less\".\n   436→\n   437→#### Test: Clicking \"Show less\" collapses the description back\n   438→- **Initial state:** User is on a property detail page with the description fully expanded and a \"Show less\" link visible.\n   439→- **Action:** User clicks the \"Show less\" link.\n   440→- **Expected:** The description collapses back to the truncated view with \"Show more\" visible again.\n   441→\n   442→#### Test: Show more/less toggle is functional on repeated use\n   443→- **Initial state:** User is on a property detail page with a long description.\n   444→- **Action:** User clicks \"Show more\", then \"Show less\", then \"Show more\" again.\n   445→- **Expected:** Each click correctly toggles between the truncated and expanded states. The final state shows the full description.\n   446→\n   447→### Component: AmenitiesList\n   448→\n   449→#### Test: Amenities list displays amenities grouped by category with icons\n   450→- **Initial state:** User navigates to `/properties/:id` for a property with amenities including \"WiFi\" (Essentials), \"Pool\" (Features), \"Smoke Detector\" (Safety), \"Near Beach\" (Location).\n   451→- **Expected:** The amenities are displayed in groups with category headings: \"Essentials\", \"Features\", \"Safety\", \"Location\". Each amenity is shown with its icon and name.\n   452→\n   453→#### Test: Amenities list only shows categories that have amenities\n   454→- **Initial state:** User navigates to a property detail page. The property has amenities only in \"Essentials\" and \"Features\" categories (none in \"Safety\" or \"Location\").\n   455→- **Expected:** Only the \"Essentials\" and \"Features\" category groups are displayed. Empty categories are not shown.\n   456→\n   457→#### Test: Amenities list shows \"Show all amenities\" when there are many amenities\n   458→- **Initial state:** User navigates to a property detail page for a property with more than 10 amenities.\n   459→- **Expected:** An initial subset of amenities is displayed with a \"Show all X amenities\" button at the bottom (where X is the total count).\n   460→\n   461→#### Test: Clicking \"Show all amenities\" reveals the complete list\n   462→- **Initial state:** User is on a property detail page with many amenities and a \"Show all X amenities\" button visible.\n   463→- **Action:** User clicks \"Show all X amenities\".\n   464→- **Expected:** All amenities are displayed, grouped by category. The button changes to \"Show less\" or disappears.\n   465→\n   466→#### Test: Amenities list displays message when property has no amenities\n   467→- **Initial state:** User navigates to a property detail page for a property with no amenities.\n   468→- **Expected:** A message like \"No amenities listed\" is displayed, or the amenities section is not shown.\n   469→\n   470→### Component: BookingCard\n   471→\n   472→#### Test: Booking card displays price per night\n   473→- **Initial state:** User navigates to `/properties/:id` for a property with price_per_night $150.\n   474→- **Expected:** The booking card (sticky sidebar on desktop) shows \"$150 / night\" prominently at the top.\n   475→\n   476→#### Test: Booking card displays check-in and check-out date pickers\n   477→- **Initial state:** User is on a property detail page.\n   478→- **Expected:** The booking card contains a check-in date picker and a check-out date picker. Both are initially empty or show placeholder text.\n   479→\n   480→#### Test: Booking card displays guest count selector\n   481→- **Initial state:** User is on a property detail page for a property with max_guests 6.\n   482→- **Expected:** The booking card contains a guest count selector. The selector enforces a minimum of 1 and a maximum of 6 (the property's max_guests value).\n   483→\n   484→#### Test: Selecting dates and guests shows price breakdown\n   485→- **Initial state:** User is on a property detail page for a property with price_per_night $150 and cleaning_fee $75.\n   486→- **Action:** User selects check-in \"2026-05-01\" and check-out \"2026-05-04\" (3 nights) and sets guests to 2.\n   487→- **Expected:** The booking card displays a price breakdown: \"$150 x 3 nights = $450\", \"Cleaning fee: $75\", \"Total: $525\". The breakdown appears after both dates are selected.\n   488→\n   489→#### Test: Price breakdown updates when dates change\n   490→- **Initial state:** User is on a property detail page with check-in \"2026-05-01\" and check-out \"2026-05-04\" selected (3 nights).\n   491→- **Action:** User changes the check-out date to \"2026-05-06\" (5 nights).\n   492→- **Expected:** The price breakdown updates to reflect 5 nights: \"$150 x 5 nights = $750\", \"Cleaning fee: $75\", \"Total: $825\".\n   493→\n   494→#### Test: Reserve button creates a booking when logged in\n   495→- **Initial state:** User is logged in, on a property detail page for another user's property. Check-in \"2026-05-01\", check-out \"2026-05-04\", and 2 guests are selected.\n   496→- **Action:** User clicks the \"Reserve\" button.\n   497→- **Expected:** The app calls `POST /api/bookings` with the property_id, check_in, check_out, num_guests, and total_price. A success message is displayed (e.g., \"Booking confirmed!\") and the user is redirected to the My Trips page (`/trips`), or a confirmation is shown on the same page.\n   498→\n   499→#### Test: Reserve button is disabled when dates are not selected"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01XeEJo91zX1zVTTDE8kgZQi","session_id":"428f3191-9775-460c-8316-8366502bc989","uuid":"03ec9201-8d41-49f9-bfd7-5a26b8d21054"}
