[2026-03-14T19:33:26.692Z] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01159LfSvvGVKJCUZiBMtmAj","type":"tool_result","content":"  1089→## Page: User Profile (`/profile`)\n  1090→\n  1091→<!-- Components: ProfileForm, BecomeHostButton, UserReviewsList -->\n  1092→\n  1093→### Component: ProfileForm\n  1094→\n  1095→#### Test: Profile page requires login\n  1096→- **Initial state:** User is not logged in.\n  1097→- **Action:** User navigates to `/profile`.\n  1098→- **Expected:** The user is redirected to `/login`. The profile page is not displayed.\n  1099→\n  1100→#### Test: Profile page displays current user info\n  1101→- **Initial state:** User is logged in with name \"Alice Smith\", email \"alice@example.com\", bio \"Love traveling!\", phone \"555-1234\", avatar URL \"https://example.com/avatar.jpg\".\n  1102→- **Action:** User navigates to `/profile`.\n  1103→- **Expected:** The profile form displays the current values: name \"Alice Smith\", email \"alice@example.com\" (read-only), bio \"Love traveling!\", phone \"555-1234\", and avatar URL \"https://example.com/avatar.jpg\". The avatar image is displayed using the URL.\n  1104→\n  1105→#### Test: Edit name field inline\n  1106→- **Initial state:** User is logged in and on `/profile` with name \"Alice Smith\".\n  1107→- **Action:** User clicks the name field, clears it, types \"Alice Johnson\", and clicks the \"Save\" button.\n  1108→- **Expected:** A `PUT /api/users/:id` request is sent with the updated name. The name field displays \"Alice Johnson\". A success message (e.g., \"Profile updated\") is shown. The Redux user state is updated with the new name.\n  1109→\n  1110→#### Test: Edit bio field inline\n  1111→- **Initial state:** User is logged in and on `/profile` with bio \"Love traveling!\".\n  1112→- **Action:** User clicks the bio textarea, clears it, types \"Digital nomad and foodie\", and clicks \"Save\".\n  1113→- **Expected:** A `PUT /api/users/:id` request is sent with the updated bio. The bio field displays \"Digital nomad and foodie\". A success message is shown.\n  1114→\n  1115→#### Test: Edit phone field inline\n  1116→- **Initial state:** User is logged in and on `/profile` with phone \"555-1234\".\n  1117→- **Action:** User clicks the phone field, clears it, types \"555-9876\", and clicks \"Save\".\n  1118→- **Expected:** A `PUT /api/users/:id` request is sent with the updated phone. The phone field displays \"555-9876\". A success message is shown.\n  1119→\n  1120→#### Test: Edit avatar URL field inline\n  1121→- **Initial state:** User is logged in and on `/profile` with avatar URL \"https://example.com/old-avatar.jpg\".\n  1122→- **Action:** User clicks the avatar URL field, clears it, types \"https://example.com/new-avatar.jpg\", and clicks \"Save\".\n  1123→- **Expected:** A `PUT /api/users/:id` request is sent with the updated avatar URL. The avatar image preview updates to show the new image from \"https://example.com/new-avatar.jpg\". A success message is shown.\n  1124→\n  1125→#### Test: Save with empty name shows validation error\n  1126→- **Initial state:** User is logged in and on `/profile`.\n  1127→- **Action:** User clears the name field (leaving it empty) and clicks \"Save\".\n  1128→- **Expected:** A validation error message is displayed (e.g., \"Name is required\"). No API call is made. The name field is highlighted as invalid.\n  1129→\n  1130→#### Test: Save with invalid avatar URL shows validation error\n  1131→- **Initial state:** User is logged in and on `/profile`.\n  1132→- **Action:** User enters \"not-a-url\" in the avatar URL field and clicks \"Save\".\n  1133→- **Expected:** A validation error message is displayed (e.g., \"Please enter a valid URL\"). No API call is made.\n  1134→\n  1135→#### Test: Profile form fields are functional on repeated edits\n  1136→- **Initial state:** User is logged in and on `/profile` with name \"Alice Smith\".\n  1137→- **Action:** User changes the name to \"Alice Johnson\" and clicks \"Save\". After the success message, user changes the name again to \"Alice Williams\" and clicks \"Save\".\n  1138→- **Expected:** Both saves succeed with separate `PUT /api/users/:id` requests. After the second save, the name field displays \"Alice Williams\". Both updates are persisted.\n  1139→\n  1140→#### Test: Email field is displayed but not editable\n  1141→- **Initial state:** User is logged in and on `/profile` with email \"alice@example.com\".\n  1142→- **Action:** User views the profile form.\n  1143→- **Expected:** The email \"alice@example.com\" is displayed but the field is read-only / disabled and cannot be edited.\n  1144→\n  1145→#### Test: Profile update persists across navigation\n  1146→- **Initial state:** User is logged in and on `/profile` with bio \"Old bio\".\n  1147→- **Action:** User changes bio to \"New bio\", clicks \"Save\", then navigates to `/` (home page), then navigates back to `/profile`.\n  1148→- **Expected:** The bio field displays \"New bio\", confirming the change was persisted to the database and Redux state.\n  1149→\n  1150→### Component: BecomeHostButton\n  1151→\n  1152→#### Test: Become a Host button is visible for non-host users\n  1153→- **Initial state:** User is logged in with `is_host` set to `false`.\n  1154→- **Action:** User navigates to `/profile`.\n  1155→- **Expected:** A \"Become a Host\" button is visible on the profile page.\n  1156→\n  1157→#### Test: Become a Host button is hidden for existing hosts\n  1158→- **Initial state:** User is logged in with `is_host` set to `true`.\n  1159→- **Action:** User navigates to `/profile`.\n  1160→- **Expected:** The \"Become a Host\" button is NOT visible on the profile page.\n  1161→\n  1162→#### Test: Clicking Become a Host sets user as host\n  1163→- **Initial state:** User is logged in with `is_host` set to `false` and on `/profile`.\n  1164→- **Action:** User clicks the \"Become a Host\" button.\n  1165→- **Expected:** A confirmation dialog appears (e.g., \"Are you sure you want to become a host?\"). User confirms. A `POST /api/users/:id/become-host` request is sent. Upon success, the button disappears, a success message is shown (e.g., \"You are now a host!\"), and the Redux user state updates `is_host` to `true`. The \"Hosting\" link becomes available in the navigation sidebar.\n  1166→\n  1167→#### Test: Cancel Become a Host confirmation dialog\n  1168→- **Initial state:** User is logged in with `is_host` set to `false` and on `/profile`. The \"Become a Host\" button is visible.\n  1169→- **Action:** User clicks the \"Become a Host\" button, then clicks \"Cancel\" in the confirmation dialog.\n  1170→- **Expected:** The dialog closes. No API call is made. The \"Become a Host\" button remains visible. `is_host` remains `false`.\n  1171→\n  1172→#### Test: Become a Host button appearance\n  1173→- **Initial state:** User is logged in with `is_host` set to `false` and on `/profile`.\n  1174→- **Action:** User views the profile page.\n  1175→- **Expected:** The \"Become a Host\" button is styled with the coral/red accent color (#FF5A5F), has clear text reading \"Become a Host\", and is visually prominent on the page.\n  1176→\n  1177→### Component: UserReviewsList\n  1178→\n  1179→#### Test: Reviews list displays user's written reviews\n  1180→- **Initial state:** User is logged in and has written 3 reviews for different properties (e.g., \"Cozy Cabin\" rated 5, \"City Apartment\" rated 3, \"Beach Villa\" rated 4).\n  1181→- **Action:** User navigates to `/profile`.\n  1182→- **Expected:** A \"My Reviews\" section is visible showing all 3 reviews. Each review card displays: the property title, the overall rating (with filled/unfilled stars), the comment text, and the date the review was written.\n  1183→\n  1184→#### Test: Reviews list shows empty state for user with no reviews\n  1185→- **Initial state:** User is logged in but has not written any reviews.\n  1186→- **Action:** User navigates to `/profile`.\n  1187→- **Expected:** The \"My Reviews\" section displays an empty state message (e.g., \"You haven't written any reviews yet\") instead of review cards.\n  1188→\n  1189→#### Test: Review card shows rating with star display\n  1190→- **Initial state:** User is logged in and has written a review with overall rating 4 out of 5.\n  1191→- **Action:** User navigates to `/profile`.\n  1192→- **Expected:** The review card displays 4 filled stars and 1 unfilled star, matching the rating value.\n  1193→\n  1194→#### Test: Review card links to the reviewed property\n  1195→- **Initial state:** User is logged in and has written a review for property \"Cozy Cabin\" (property ID \"abc-123\").\n  1196→- **Action:** User clicks on the property title \"Cozy Cabin\" in a review card.\n  1197→- **Expected:** The user is navigated to `/properties/abc-123` (the property detail page for \"Cozy Cabin\").\n  1198→\n  1199→#### Test: Reviews list shows review details correctly\n  1200→- **Initial state:** User is logged in and has written a review with rating 5, comment \"Amazing stay! The host was very welcoming.\", for property \"Beach Villa\", dated \"2026-01-15\".\n  1201→- **Action:** User navigates to `/profile`.\n  1202→- **Expected:** The review card displays: property title \"Beach Villa\", 5 filled stars, comment text \"Amazing stay! The host was very welcoming.\", and date \"Jan 15, 2026\".\n  1203→\n  1204→#### Test: Reviews list updates after writing a new review\n  1205→- **Initial state:** User is logged in, on `/profile`, and has 2 existing reviews displayed.\n  1206→- **Action:** User navigates to a completed booking, writes a new review, submits it, then navigates back to `/profile`.\n  1207→- **Expected:** The \"My Reviews\" section now displays 3 reviews, including the newly written review with the correct property title, rating, and comment.\n  1208→\n  1209→#### Test: Reviews list shows multiple reviews in chronological order\n  1210→- **Initial state:** User is logged in and has written reviews on different dates: \"Beach Villa\" on 2026-01-15, \"City Apartment\" on 2026-02-10, \"Cozy Cabin\" on 2026-03-05.\n  1211→- **Action:** User navigates to `/profile`.\n  1212→- **Expected:** The reviews are displayed in reverse chronological order (newest first): \"Cozy Cabin\" (Mar 5, 2026), \"City Apartment\" (Feb 10, 2026), \"Beach Villa\" (Jan 15, 2026).\n  1213→\n  1214→## Page: Write Review (`/trips/:bookingId/review`)\n  1215→\n  1216→<!-- Components: ReviewForm, RatingSliders, PropertyBookingContext -->\n  1217→\n  1218→### Component: PropertyBookingContext\n  1219→\n  1220→#### Test: Property info displays for the booking being reviewed\n  1221→- **Initial state:** User \"guest@example.com\" is logged in and has a completed booking (booking-789) for \"Oceanfront Villa\" in Malibu, CA with check-in 2026-01-10 and check-out 2026-01-15.\n  1222→- **Action:** User navigates to `/trips/booking-789/review`.\n  1223→- **Expected:** The page displays the property context section showing the property title \"Oceanfront Villa\", the location \"Malibu, CA\", the property's main image, check-in date \"Jan 10, 2026\", check-out date \"Jan 15, 2026\", and the number of nights (5 nights).\n  1224→\n  1225→#### Test: Property booking context shows guest count\n  1226→- **Initial state:** User is logged in with a completed booking (booking-789) for 3 guests at \"Oceanfront Villa\".\n  1227→- **Action:** User navigates to `/trips/booking-789/review`.\n  1228→- **Expected:** The property booking context section displays \"3 guests\" alongside the booking dates.\n  1229→\n  1230→#### Test: Property booking context shows total price paid\n  1231→- **Initial state:** User is logged in with a completed booking (booking-789) with a total_price of $1,250.\n  1232→- **Action:** User navigates to `/trips/booking-789/review`.\n  1233→- **Expected:** The property booking context displays the total price \"$1,250\" that was paid for the booking.\n  1234→\n  1235→#### Test: Redirect to login if not authenticated\n  1236→- **Initial state:** No user is logged in.\n  1237→- **Action:** User navigates to `/trips/booking-789/review`.\n  1238→- **Expected:** The app redirects the user to `/login`. The Write Review page is not displayed.\n  1239→\n  1240→#### Test: Error state when booking does not exist\n  1241→- **Initial state:** User \"guest@example.com\" is logged in.\n  1242→- **Action:** User navigates to `/trips/nonexistent-booking-id/review`.\n  1243→- **Expected:** The page displays an error message such as \"Booking not found\" and does not show the review form.\n  1244→\n  1245→#### Test: Error state when booking belongs to another user\n  1246→- **Initial state:** User \"other@example.com\" is logged in. Booking booking-789 belongs to \"guest@example.com\".\n  1247→- **Action:** User navigates to `/trips/booking-789/review`.\n  1248→- **Expected:** The page displays an error message such as \"You cannot review this booking\" and does not show the review form.\n  1249→\n  1250→#### Test: Error state when booking is not completed\n  1251→- **Initial state:** User \"guest@example.com\" is logged in with a booking (booking-pending) that has status \"pending\".\n  1252→- **Action:** User navigates to `/trips/booking-pending/review`.\n  1253→- **Expected:** The page displays an error message such as \"You can only review completed bookings\" and does not show the review form.\n  1254→\n  1255→#### Test: Error state when review already exists for booking\n  1256→- **Initial state:** User \"guest@example.com\" is logged in with a completed booking (booking-reviewed) that already has a review submitted.\n  1257→- **Action:** User navigates to `/trips/booking-reviewed/review`.\n  1258→- **Expected:** The page displays a message such as \"You have already reviewed this booking\" and does not show the review form. Optionally shows a link back to My Trips.\n  1259→\n  1260→### Component: RatingSliders\n  1261→\n  1262→#### Test: All six rating sliders display with default values\n  1263→- **Initial state:** User is logged in and navigates to `/trips/booking-789/review` for a completed booking.\n  1264→- **Expected:** Six rating sliders are visible with labels: \"Overall\", \"Cleanliness\", \"Accuracy\", \"Communication\", \"Location\", and \"Value\". Each slider defaults to a mid-range value (e.g., 3 out of 5) or is unset, and shows the current numeric value.\n  1265→\n  1266→#### Test: Adjust overall rating slider\n  1267→- **Initial state:** User is on the Write Review page with all sliders at default.\n  1268→- **Action:** User drags the \"Overall\" slider to 5.\n  1269→- **Expected:** The \"Overall\" slider displays value 5. The numeric display next to the slider updates to \"5\". Other sliders remain at their previous values.\n  1270→\n  1271→#### Test: Adjust cleanliness rating slider\n  1272→- **Initial state:** User is on the Write Review page with all sliders at default.\n  1273→- **Action:** User drags the \"Cleanliness\" slider to 4.\n  1274→- **Expected:** The \"Cleanliness\" slider displays value 4. The numeric display updates to \"4\".\n  1275→\n  1276→#### Test: Adjust accuracy rating slider\n  1277→- **Initial state:** User is on the Write Review page with all sliders at default.\n  1278→- **Action:** User drags the \"Accuracy\" slider to 2.\n  1279→- **Expected:** The \"Accuracy\" slider displays value 2. The numeric display updates to \"2\".\n  1280→\n  1281→#### Test: Adjust communication rating slider\n  1282→- **Initial state:** User is on the Write Review page with all sliders at default.\n  1283→- **Action:** User drags the \"Communication\" slider to 5.\n  1284→- **Expected:** The \"Communication\" slider displays value 5. The numeric display updates to \"5\".\n  1285→\n  1286→#### Test: Adjust location rating slider\n  1287→- **Initial state:** User is on the Write Review page with all sliders at default.\n  1288→- **Action:** User drags the \"Location\" slider to 3."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01XeEJo91zX1zVTTDE8kgZQi","session_id":"428f3191-9775-460c-8316-8366502bc989","uuid":"35ff4bc6-b664-4d6b-821e-1d6a55cebdee"}
